+/// HOW MANY RUNS ONE POOL JOB HANDS OVER AT A TIME.
+///
+/// A chunk is the unit of both balancing and hand-off.  The rule the merger
+/// obeys is "add run i only after every run before i has been added", so a
+/// chunk that finishes early has to WAIT — which means the size of the wait
+/// queue, not the size of the row, is what bounds the shards in flight.  At
+/// roughly thirty chunks per lane a lane still gets plenty of chances to pick
+/// up the next chunk, so balance stays within a chunk or two.
+fn chunk_for(n: usize, lanes: usize) -> usize {
+    ((n + lanes * 32 - 1) / (lanes * 32)).max(1)
+}
